    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `locality` field is derived from the city via the fixed table and exposed on the `GET /api/owners/{id}` JSON. I kept structural impact low by adding behaviour as a small cohesive unit rather than growing any existing class:\n\n1. **New `util/Localities.java`** \u2014 a self-contained helper (mirroring the existing `Addresses`/`E164` utilities) with one simple method `regionOf(city)` that does a `Map.getOrDefault(..., \"UNKNOWN\")` lookup over the pinned table `Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD`. WMC_other \u2248 0, CC = 1.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `locality` read-only property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field automatically.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line on `toOwnerDto`, following the exact pattern already used for `membershipTier`, delegating to `Localities.regionOf(owner.getCity())`.\n\nNo changes to the large `Owner` model or the controller, so the high-WMC classes were left untouched.",
